posts.body:
Mm, so it sounds like you need to do two things; after catching a monster (with the first plugin), check to see if the party has more than 6 members, and if it does automatically trigger the second plugin to store the most recently caught monster.
Looking at the thread for the second plugin, people have said that the script call
$gameSystem.depositedActors.push(X);
(where X is the ID of the actor in question from the database) will store that actor. (Possibly you also need to use
$gameParty.removeActor(X);
to remove them from your current party? Not sure, I haven't tested).
So, what we need to do is run some code after you catch an enemy to check the number of people in the party - I believe the script call for that is
if($gameParty.members().length > 6)
and then grab the actor ID of the last member:
$gameParty.members()[6].actorId()
and then use the
$gameSystem.depositedActors.push(X);
to deposit them.
Put it all together, I think it would look like this (though again, this is untested!):
Code:
if($gameParty.members().length > 6) {
var actor = $gameParty.members()[6].actorId();
$gameSystem.depositedActors.push(actor);
}
Run that snippet after every time you catch a monster, and hopefully it will work. Like I said, you might need to use
Code:
if($gameParty.members().length > 6) {
var actor = $gameParty.members()[6].actorId();
$gameSystem.depositedActors.push(actor);
$gameParty.removeActor(actor);
}
if it's storing them but not also removing a version from the party.

